###    result
Confirmed empirically. Here's the full answer to both ideas.

## 1. Alignments = Clear Bible bible_alignments — 10 languages, but no Chinese

It's word-level alignment data (Scripture Burrito format) mapping each original Hebrew/Greek token (which carries the Strong's number) to target-language words. Languages present: arb, asm, ben, eng, fra, hau, hin, por, rus, spa (10). UNV/Chinese is NOT in it.

So its value for A2 is not "more source texts to project from" — piling 10 source languages into the model's prompt would re-create survey6's info-overload failure. Its real value is as a scoring-side tool: the alignment tells us, per Strong's number, which of the 10 languages actually expresses it. An SN that few languages align to = Hebrew morphology/particle → a principled signal for the exclusion list.

## 2. Exclusion list / intersection-only scoring — your hunch is confirmed

I diffed the real FHL Strong's sets on Gen 1:1:

| | Strong's set |
|---|---|
| **UNV** | 430, 776, 853, 1254, 7225, 8064, **09002** |
| **KJV** | 430, 776, 853, 1254, 7225, 8064 |
| **UNV-only (unfair to score)** | **09002** ← the ב inseparable prefix ("in") |
| **SHARED (fair A2 set)** | 430, 776, 853, 1254, 7225, 8064 |

The single UNV-only SN is exactly a 09xxx-family prefix — your "9xxx族" intuition, dead on. KJV/English has no separate token for the Hebrew ב prefix, so projecting from KJV can never produce 09002 on UNV → scoring it would penalize the model for something the source can't supply. (Note: 0853 את and 8804 morphology happened to be tagged in KJV here too, so they're shared on this verse — the exclusion is verse-specific, not a fixed blanket.)

So the divide-and-conquer is right: per verse, score placement only on UNV_FHL_SN ∩ source_SN, and exclude the UNV-only set (mostly 09xxx prefixes, plus case-by-case 0853/8xxx) as "out of scope — source can't supply it."

Two ways to build the exclusion, cheap→robust:
- Rule-based (matches the project's own token classification): drop 09xxx prefixes (+ 0853/8xxx when the source lacks them), keep Core content SNs. Zero API cost.
- Empirical (what I just did): per verse, diff UNV-FHL vs KJV-FHL → the UNV-only set is the exclusion. Optionally cross-check against the 10-language alignment's expression-rate to catch non-obvious cases.

## Recommendation

For A2 I'd wire a small build_exclusion.py: per verse compute shared = UNV∩KJV, score s1/s10 placement only on shared, and report the excluded morphology/prefix SNs separately. That gives a clean, fair, leak-free placement contest — exactly your 分而治之.

Want me to build that exclusion + scoring scaffold now (it's cheap and de-risks A2), or fold this into S10_VS_S1_GOLD_EXPERIMENT.md first?




